# @name forgotPasswordDifferentCase
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "email": "ADMIN@AMANIX.COM"
}

### =====================================================================
### 2.9 PHASE 0 REGRESSION SUITE (P0-1 / P0-2)
### =====================================================================
### Unlike the sections above, these requests carry explicit `?? status` assertions. A request with
### no assertion cannot fail a `--bail` run, so this section exists to fail loudly if either defect
### is reintroduced.
###
### P0-1: ChangePasswordCommandHandler called Verify(hash, plainText) against a
###       Verify(plainText, hash) signature, so every password change silently failed.
### P0-2: LoginCommandHandler never issued a refresh token, so /auth/refresh-token could never
###       succeed for a freshly logged-in user.
### See Docs/ai/12_ENGINEERING_BACKLOG_AND_TECH_DEBT.md
###
### NOTE ON FIELD CASING: the API serializes camelCase (no JsonSerializerOptions naming policy is
### configured, so ASP.NET Core's default applies). Verified against a running instance:
###   {"isSuccess":true,"message":"...","data":{"token":"...","refreshToken":"...", ...}}
### This section therefore reads `data.token` / `data.refreshToken`, NOT the PascalCase paths used
### elsewhere in these suites — see tech-debt item D-8.
###
### Self-contained and state-restoring: changes a password and changes it back, so it can run in
### any order without breaking the suites that follow.

@p0TempPassword = P0Regression@2026

### 2.9.1 [P0-2] Login must return BOTH an access token and a refresh token
# @name p0Login
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "email": "{{superAdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{superAdminPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

@p0AccessToken = {{p0Login.data.token}}
@p0RefreshToken = {{p0Login.data.refreshToken}}

### 2.9.2 [P0-2] The refresh token issued at login must be redeemable (proves it was persisted)
# @name p0Refresh
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "accessToken": "{{p0AccessToken}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{p0RefreshToken}}"
}

?? status == 200

### 2.9.3 [P0-2] Replaying the now-superseded refresh token must be rejected (rotation enforced)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "accessToken": "{{p0AccessToken}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{p0RefreshToken}}"
}

?? status == 400

### 2.9.4 [P0-1] Change password with the WRONG current password must be rejected
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/me/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{p0AccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "currentPassword": "ThisIsNotTheCurrentPassword@9",
  "newPassword": "{{p0TempPassword}}"
}

?? status == 400

### 2.9.5 [P0-1] Change password with the CORRECT current password must succeed
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/me/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{p0AccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "currentPassword": "{{superAdminPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{p0TempPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

### 2.9.6 [P0-1] The NEW password must now authenticate — proves the change actually took effect
# @name p0LoginWithNewPassword
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "email": "{{superAdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{p0TempPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

@p0NewAccessToken = {{p0LoginWithNewPassword.data.token}}

### 2.9.7 [P0-1] The OLD password must no longer authenticate
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "email": "{{superAdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{superAdminPassword}}"
}

?? status == 400

### 2.9.8 [CLEANUP] Restore the original password so this section is order-independent
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/me/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{p0NewAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "currentPassword": "{{p0TempPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{superAdminPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

### =====================================================================
### 2.10 LOGOUT — ENDING THE SESSION ON THE SERVER
### =====================================================================
### Signing out has to revoke the refresh token. Otherwise a token copied from a shared machine
### keeps working for its full lifetime after the user believes they have signed out.

### 2.10.1 Sign in to get a session to end
# @name logoutFlowLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{tenantManagerEmail}}", "password": "{{tenantManagerPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@logoutFlowAccessToken = {{logoutFlowLogin.data.token}}
@logoutFlowRefreshToken = {{logoutFlowLogin.data.refreshToken}}

### 2.10.2 Log out -> 200
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{logoutFlowAccessToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200

### 2.10.3 The refresh token no longer works -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "accessToken": "{{logoutFlowAccessToken}}", "refreshToken": "{{logoutFlowRefreshToken}}" }

?? status == 400

### 2.10.4 Logging out again is still a success (idempotent)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{logoutFlowAccessToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200

### 2.10.5 Logging out without a token -> 401
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/logout

?? status == 401
